/-!
# Birational Cartier pullback and geometric reduction

Source: ILO, Travaux de Gabber, Expose X, §2.3 Step 1, printed p. 150;
Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 02OO and Varieties, Tag 04KS
(blueprint: lem-sfb-birational-cartier-geometric-reduction).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace
open scoped TensorProduct

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Birational replacements of a geometrically reduced component preserve geometric
reducedness and Cartier markings. A reduced closed immersion with image Z is the reduced
induced component: this is the uniqueness clause of
`lem-weil-pbc-reduced-induced-closed-subscheme`. The integral instance on T₀ records the
node's assertion that these birational maps are between nonempty integral schemes.
The three algebra-map equalities specify the canonical base-field action on each generic
stalk; these are choices of notation for already determined algebra structures.

Source: ILO, Travaux de Gabber, Expose X, §2.3 Step 1, printed p. 150; Stacks Project,
Divisors, Tag 02OO and Varieties, Tag 04KS
(blueprint: lem-sfb-birational-cartier-geometric-reduction).

Proof:
1. On an affine chart of the chosen reduced component, the component is cut out by a
minimal prime, by `lem-weil-pbc-spec-irreducible-closed-subsets-primes` and
`def-weil-irreducible-components`. The affine description from
`lem-weil-pbc-reduced-induced-closed-subscheme` and the field localization in
`lem-weil-pbc-minimal-prime-reduced-localization-field` identify that localization with the
component function field, using `lem-sc-integral-function-field-affine-fraction`.
2. After every field extension, tensoring the reduced chart and localizing shows that the
component function field has reduced tensor product, using
`lem-weil-pbc-open-immersion-base-change`, `lem-weil-pbc-fibre-product-affine-spectra`,
`def-pc-reduced-scheme` and `lem-weil-pbc-localization-tensor-over-base`.
A localization of a reduced ring is reduced: if (a/s)^n = 0, a denominator t kills a^n;
then (ta)^n = 0, so ta = 0 and a/s = 0.
3. Dense-open birational identifications induce the corresponding generic-stalk/function-
field identifications, so the same reduced tensor products hold for the two birational
models (`def-sc-function-field`, `def-weil-pbc-module-stalk`,
`lem-sc-integral-function-field-affine-fraction`, `def-weil-open-immersion`).
4. The generic-stalk criterion for geometric reducedness gives geometric reducedness of
both integral models, by `lem-pur-geometric-reducedness-from-generic-stalks` and
`def-pc-integral-scheme`; no finite-type hypothesis on the models is needed.
5. A dominant morphism between integral schemes sends the generic point to the generic
point and induces injective maps on affine coordinate rings. Indeed the generic stalk
map is an injective field map and the germs from both affine rings are injective, by
`lem-sc-integral-function-field-affine-fraction` and `def-weil-pbc-module-stalk`.
6. On affine Cartier charts, the pullback ideal is generated by the image of the Cartier
generator, by the fibre-product quotient computation B tensor_R R/(t) = B/(image t).
Use `def-nagata-effective-cartier-ideal`, `lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-ideal-closed-subscheme`,
`lem-weil-pbc-fibre-product-affine-spectra`, `lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-base-change`,
`def-sbc-closed-immersion-ideal-sheaf` and `def-nagata-extended-ideal`.
7. Dominance and integrality keep that image nonzero in every nonempty affine chart; hence
it is a nonzerodivisor, by `def-nagata-effective-cartier-ideal` and
`def-pc-integral-scheme`. The vanishing set is the inverse image of the original one since
the affine point map contracts primes. Apply this also to h, whose dense-open
identification makes it dominant. The unit ideal and its empty vanishing set are allowed.
-/
theorem birational_cartier_geometric_reduction
    (e : Type u) [Field e]
    (T : Scheme.{u}) [T.Over (Spec (.of e))]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (T ↘ Spec (.of e))]
    [QuasiCompact (T ↘ Spec (.of e))]
    [GeometricallyReduced (T ↘ Spec (.of e))]
    (Z : Set T) (hZ : Z ∈ irreducibleComponents T)
    (T₀ : Scheme.{u}) [T₀.Over (Spec (.of e))] [IsIntegral T₀]
    (i₀ : T₀ ⟶ T) [IsClosedImmersion i₀]
    (hi₀ : Set.range i₀ = Z)
    (hi₀e : i₀ ≫ (T ↘ Spec (.of e)) = T₀ ↘ Spec (.of e))
    (S N : Scheme.{u})
    [S.Over (Spec (.of e))] [N.Over (Spec (.of e))]
    [IsIntegral S] [IsIntegral N]
    (b : S ⟶ T₀)
    (hb : b ≫ (T₀ ↘ Spec (.of e)) = S ↘ Spec (.of e))
    (Ub : T₀.Opens) (Vb : S.Opens) (eb : Vb.toScheme ≅ Ub.toScheme)
    (hUb : Dense (Ub : Set T₀)) (hVb : Dense (Vb : Set S))
    (heb : eb.hom ≫ Ub.ι = Vb.ι ≫ b)
    (h : N ⟶ S)
    (hh : h ≫ (S ↘ Spec (.of e)) = N ↘ Spec (.of e))
    (Uh : S.Opens) (Wh : N.Opens) (eh : Wh.toScheme ≅ Uh.toScheme)
    (hUh : Dense (Uh : Set S)) (hWh : Dense (Wh : Set N))
    (heh : eh.hom ≫ Uh.ι = Wh.ι ≫ h)
    [Algebra e T₀.functionField] [Algebra e S.functionField] [Algebra e N.functionField]
    (haT₀ : algebraMap e T₀.functionField =
      (StructureSheaf.toStalk e ((T₀ ↘ Spec (.of e)) (genericPoint T₀)) ≫
        (T₀ ↘ Spec (.of e)).stalkMap (genericPoint T₀)).hom)
    (haS : algebraMap e S.functionField =
      (StructureSheaf.toStalk e ((S ↘ Spec (.of e)) (genericPoint S)) ≫
        (S ↘ Spec (.of e)).stalkMap (genericPoint S)).hom)
    (haN : algebraMap e N.functionField =
      (StructureSheaf.toStalk e ((N ↘ Spec (.of e)) (genericPoint N)) ≫
        (N ↘ Spec (.of e)).stalkMap (genericPoint N)).hom)
    (J : S.IdealSheafData) (hJ : J.IsInvertible) :
    GeometricallyReduced (S ↘ Spec (.of e)) ∧
      GeometricallyReduced (N ↘ Spec (.of e)) ∧
      (J.comap h).IsInvertible ∧
      (J.comap h).support = J.support.preimage h.continuous ∧
      (∀ (Y : Scheme.{u}) [IsIntegral Y] (g : Y ⟶ S) [IsDominant g],
        (J.comap g).IsInvertible ∧
        (J.comap g).support = J.support.preimage g.continuous) ∧
      (∃ (hbη : b (genericPoint S) = genericPoint T₀)
          (hhη : h (genericPoint N) = genericPoint S),
        Function.Bijective
          (((T₀.presheaf.stalkCongr (Inseparable.of_eq hbη)).inv ≫
            b.stalkMap (genericPoint S) : T₀.functionField ⟶ S.functionField)) ∧
        Function.Bijective
          (((S.presheaf.stalkCongr (Inseparable.of_eq hhη)).inv ≫
            h.stalkMap (genericPoint N) : S.functionField ⟶ N.functionField))) ∧
      ∀ (L : Type u) [Field L] [Algebra e L],
        _root_.IsReduced (S.functionField ⊗[e] L) ∧
        _root_.IsReduced (N.functionField ⊗[e] L) ∧
        _root_.IsReduced (T₀.functionField ⊗[e] L) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
